HolonomicSystems -- Examples of Holonomic D-modules
***************************************************

Description
===========

Some examples of D-modules

  * *note gkz: gkz, -- create the A-hypergeometric system of Gelfand, Kapranov
    and Zelevinsky (GKZ)
  * *note eulerOperators: eulerOperators, -- Euler Operators
  * *note toricIdealPartials: toricIdealPartials, -- create the toric ideal of
    an integer matrix
  * *note AppellF1: AppellF1, -- Appell F1 system of PDE's

*note Canonical Series Tutorial: Canonical Series Tutorial, -- Computing series
solutions to regular holonomic systems

  * *note distraction: distraction, -- the image in the thetaRing of a
    torus-fixed element or ideal in a Weyl algebra
  * *note cssExpts: cssExpts, -- the exponents of the canonical series
    solutions of I in the direction of a weight vector
  * *note cssExptsMult: cssExptsMult, -- the exponents and multiplicities of
    the canonical series solutions
  * *note isTorusFixed: isTorusFixed, -- checks if an ideal in a Weyl algebra
    is torus-fixed
  * *note solveFrobeniusIdeal: solveFrobeniusIdeal, -- solving Frobenius ideals

Differential Operators

  * *note diffOps: diffOps, -- differential operators of up to the given order
    for a quotient polynomial ring
* Menu:

* gkz::                         create the A-hypergeometric system of Gelfand, Kapranov and Zelevinsky (GKZ)
* eulerOperators::              Euler Operators
* toricIdealPartials::          create the toric ideal of an integer matrix
* AppellF1::                    Appell F1 system of PDE's
* Canonical Series Tutorial::   Computing series solutions to regular holonomic systems
* diffOps::                     differential operators of up to the given order for a quotient polynomial ring

