indicialIdeal -- the image in the thetaRing of an indicial ideal in a Weyl algebra
**********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        indicialIdeal(I,w)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, in a WeylAlgebra that is
        torus-fixed
      * w, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, (generic) weights for $I$, of
        length half the number of variables in the Weyl algebra
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, that results from intersecting
        with the thetaRing of D with the result of extending the ideal
        in_(-w,w)(I) with the rational function field in the Weyl algebra
        variables, as in [SST (see
        https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/pdf/1734566.pdf ), Theorem 2.3.9]
        to I.

Description
===========

