isTorusFixed -- checks if an ideal in a Weyl algebra is torus-fixed
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isTorusFixed I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, in a WeylAlgebra
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, true if I is
        torus-fixed, false if not

Description
===========

There is a natural action of the n-dimensional algebraic torus on $D$ where $t
\in (\mathbb{C}^*)^n$ acts on $\partial_i$ as $t_i\partial_i$ and on $x_i$ as
$t_i^{-1}x_i$. The function isTorusFixed verifies whether a D-ideal is
invariant under this action.

See [SST (see https://mathscinet.ams.org/mathscinet/pdf/1734566.pdf )], just
before Lemma 2.3.1.

