diffOps -- differential operators of up to the given order for a quotient polynomial ring
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        diffOps (I, k)
        diffOps (f, k)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, contained in a polynomial ring
        R
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, an element of a
        polynomial ring R
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, which is nonnegative
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, the differential
        operators of order at most k of the quotient ring R/I (or R/(f))

Description
===========

Given an ideal $I$ of a polynomial ring $R$ the set of differential operators
of the quotient ring $R/I$ having order less than or equal to $k$ forms a
finitely generated module over $R/I$. This routine returns its generating set.



The output is in the form of a hash table. The key BasisElts is a row vector of
basic differential operators. The key PolyGens is a matrix over R whose column
vectors represent differential operators of R/I in the following way.  For each
column vector, consider its image in R/I then take its dot product with the
BasisElts. This gives a differential operator, and the set of these operators
generates the differential operators of R/I of order k or less as an
(R/I)-module.

